# Agent-owned delivery (Dominik + Cursor)

## Roles

| Dominik | Cursor agent |
|---------|----------------|
| Product and scope decisions | Implement features and fixes end-to-end |
| Optional production smoke test | Commit, push, PR, merge after CI green |
| | Run tests/build; deploy via `scripts/deploy-prod.sh` |
| | DE/EN copy, i18n, minimal diff |

## Agent ships by default

After implementation and tests pass, the agent **commits, pushes, opens a PR, and merges when CI is green** — without waiting for a separate “commit for me” instruction.

Pause before ship only when:

- Scope is ambiguous (auth, migrations, API contract) — ask first
- Destructive git ops (force push, hard reset) — ask first
- Dominik explicitly says “don’t deploy yet”, “plan only”, or “just explain” in that turn

## Deploy policy

| Change type | Merge to main | Deploy to production |
|-------------|---------------|----------------------|
| Backend, migration, widget, notifications | Yes | **Immediately** after merge |
| Feature with user-visible behavior (inbox, settings, chat) | Yes | **Immediately** after merge |
| UI/copy/i18n-only fix (no runtime logic) | Yes | **Batch** — deploy when 2+ small fixes are on `main`, or Dominik asks to deploy |

Bundled deploy: `./scripts/deploy-prod.sh frontend` for frontend-only batch; full deploy when backend is included.

## Git and workspace

- **Git operations:** `~/dev/ai-business-platform` (healthy clone)
- **Edits:** Desktop workspace or dev clone; run `./scripts/sync-from-desktop.sh` (desktop → dev) before commit if editing on desktop
- `git pull origin main` before branching

## Task handoff

Brief confirmation: what shipped, PR link, deploy now or batched, 1–3 DE smoke-test bullets when deployed.

## Default PR size

One owner-visible outcome per change. No drive-by refactors.
